All eight fixes are in, and `npm test` passes: worker 47/47 in 7 files, plus a clean `tsc` typecheck, and extension 36/36. I couldn't run `npm run test:e2e` here. Chromium won't start because the system library `libatk-1.0.so.0` is missing, and I don't have the permissions to install it. That run needs to be repeated on a machine that has Playwright's browser dependencies. Nothing was committed, pushed or deployed, and `release/` and the secrets weren't touched.

**Changes:**
1. **`extension/background.js`:** `BATCH` is now 5. On a 413, sync retries that batch one page at a time. A page that still gets a 413 on its own is removed from the queue and marked `failed: 'too large'` in the recent list, so the same batch can't be retried forever. Other errors stop the sync as before. The send and queue-cleanup code moved into two small helpers inside `doSync`.
2. **`worker/src/mcp.ts`:** `list_pages` now adds the same untrusted-content notice line and `untrusted: true` that `search_memory` uses, whenever it returns any pages.
3. **`extension/content.js`:** `getSettings()` reads only `paused`, `blocklist` and `workerUrl`, so content scripts never read the secret. The background script still checks the secret before anything is stored or sent.
4. **`worker/src/search.ts`:** `forget()` removes duplicate ids with `new Set()` and returns `{deleted: 0}` for an empty list before building the `IN (...)` query.
5. **`ghost:test-capture`:** nothing in `tests/` sends this event, so I gated it. The listener is only added when `chrome.storage.local.testHooks === true`, and it uses the same `capture()` path with the same privacy checks.
6. **Accessibility:**
   - **`extension/onboarding.html` and `onboarding.css`:** each step dot now contains visually hidden "Step N of 3" text.
   - **`worker/src/landing.ts`:** `button` and `.btn` get a `:focus-visible` outline.
7. **`README.md`:**
   - The S11a and S11b rows now say `703d62b`, and a new S12 row (Firefox build) uses the same hash. `git log` shows S11 and S12 landed in that one commit.
   - s12 is listed under Logs & Prompts.
   - Added the judges note about a fresh Chrome profile and pausing or removing the extension, and the Kiro Features Used table.
   - Added the free-tier line about D1 vectors being scanned on every query, so use Vectorize past roughly 1,000-2,000 pages.
   - Added a short mention of the new `mcp.json` in the Kiro CLI section.
8. **`.kiro/settings/mcp.json` (new):** it points at `https://<your-worker>.workers.dev/mcp` with the header `Authorization: Bearer ${GHOST_SECRET}`. It has `"disabled": true` so Kiro doesn't try to connect to the placeholder address until the user fills in their own.

**Already in the working tree before I started:** uncommitted edits in `.gitignore`, `extension/lib/blocklist.js`, `extension/lib/redact.js`, `extension/test/privacy.test.mjs` and `worker/src/ingest.ts`, plus an untracked `worker/test/ingest.test.ts`. That extra test file is why the worker count is 47 tests in 7 files. The README still says 45 tests in 6 files, and I didn't update that.
